  {
   "id": "c7cd34f3b4b8d623",
   "entity": "code-quantumn",
   "url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/13/geoffrey-huntley/",
   "canonical_url": "https://simonwillison.net/2026/Oct/13/geoffrey-huntley",
   "title": "Quoting Geoffrey Huntley",
   "snippet": "If the agent isn't using my diagnostics library, I could introspect and update AGENTS.md, but there's still a delta, and it'll drift. Instead, I write a pre-commit hook that checks the git diff for direct calls to observability modules that bypass my diagnostics module. Boom: fail the commit, inject a prompt telling the agent to use the diagnostics library. All of a sudden it's ten out of ten. — G",
